  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper presents a gate-based variational portfolio optimization method using Pauli Correlation Encoding (PCE) with a Hardware-Efficient Ansatz, evaluated on S&P 500 graphs of size m = 10, 20, 30, 50, 100, 150, 200, and 250. It reports PCE gate counts of 25, 61, 91, 145/148, 295/298, 433/430, 595/586, and 730/715 for k = 3/k = 2, respectively, and states that the method can solve m >= 200 in about one hour on a statevector simulator; however, no practical quantum advantage over classical baselines is demonstrated.",
